      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Authentication Provider**\n\nOkay, I've decided to use Firebase Authentication for `register_user.py`. It provides a good balance of features and ease of integration for email/password authentication. I need to make sure this is clearly reflected in the code itself, to aid readability and maintainability.\n\n\n**Implementing Registration Logic**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing the `register_user.py` file with Firebase. I'm making sure to keep the Firebase-specific code visible for easy identification, which I'll achieve by importing `firebase_admin.auth` and using `auth.create_user`. I've decided to assume that the user will install the SDKs needed for the chosen provider if they haven't already, so no import checks are in the source code. I need to make sure I handle errors gracefully, such as email already existing. I'll focus on producing the bare-bones code.\n\n\n**Defining Registration File**\n\nI'm now creating `register_user.py` using Firebase. I'll include the Firebase Admin SDK initialization using a placeholder for the service account key path, and the firebase project ID, which the user will populate. I will also be defining the `register_user` function with error handling. This is ready to be delivered.\n\n\n",
